                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>is it in the Seminole area? Seminole. It’s Seminole County. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406826" ANNOTATION_REF="a406825">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So did you all live in town? Or--No, not that. The town, you know,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406828" ANNOTATION_REF="a406827">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>in the woods, as you would say, or prairie. Did they used to call it in the country? Uh-huh. In the country. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406830" ANNOTATION_REF="a406829">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then, uh</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406832" ANNOTATION_REF="a406831">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>your family that lived there, your mother and your father, how many kids lived there? Uh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406834" ANNOTATION_REF="a406833">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The close family. Nine.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406836" ANNOTATION_REF="a406835">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>There used to be nine of us, but two passed away, and now,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406838" ANNOTATION_REF="a406837">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>there are just two of us left, uh-huh, those children. How many boys were there?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406840" ANNOTATION_REF="a406839">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>There were two boys--oh-oh, there were three.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406842" ANNOTATION_REF="a406841">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>One little boy that was about two years old, might have been one, passed away. And how about the girls?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406844" ANNOTATION_REF="a406843">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The girls--How many of you all were there? Eight, it might have been five, one passed away also</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406846" ANNOTATION_REF="a406845">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>uh</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406848" ANNOTATION_REF="a406847">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>as we went on, another would pass away,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406850" ANNOTATION_REF="a406849">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>now just two are left, women. Juanita and-- Juanita, that’s my sister.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406852" ANNOTATION_REF="a406851">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Is she the one they call the baby of the family?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406854" ANNOTATION_REF="a406853">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Isn’t she the baby sister? That’s right. She’s the youngest one?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406856" ANNOTATION_REF="a406855">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Juanita’s the baby. Oh, my goodness. That’s all right. She was the baby.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406858" ANNOTATION_REF="a406857">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So when you lived in the country or woods and grew up, your father or your mother, which one worked?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406860" ANNOTATION_REF="a406859">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh, neither one worked. </ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406862" ANNOTATION_REF="a406861">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>My moth--my father was what they used to call a farmer. He grew crops. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406864" ANNOTATION_REF="a406863">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He worked and plowed and grew crops,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406866" ANNOTATION_REF="a406865">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and he made us work as we were growing up. Oh. What kind of crops did he grow?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406868" ANNOTATION_REF="a406867">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Corn and beans, all the vegetables you can think of. Wow. Was it a big field? Uh-huh. The fields of them were big.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406870" ANNOTATION_REF="a406869">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh, what is it? What’s the name?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406872" ANNOTATION_REF="a406871">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He had vegetables, too</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406874" ANNOTATION_REF="a406873">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Greens? Uh-huh. Like onions, too? He grew cotton, too.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406876" ANNOTATION_REF="a406875">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He grew peanuts and things, too. Wow. And corn. And what about tomatoes?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406878" ANNOTATION_REF="a406877">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Tomatoes and those things, uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406880" ANNOTATION_REF="a406879">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He would grow all the things you could eat, and we would can them and put them up. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406882" ANNOTATION_REF="a406881">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>When it got cold and became winter time, we would eat and live there.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406884" ANNOTATION_REF="a406883">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And what about meats, the cattle, the pigs? Those too, we had pigs, and cattle</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406886" ANNOTATION_REF="a406885">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>what they used to call milk [cows], we would milk them, just my brothers would milk them.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406888" ANNOTATION_REF="a406887">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Was that their chore? Uh-huh, that was their chore.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406890" ANNOTATION_REF="a406889">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He was a minister, too. Uh-huh. Oh, your father?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406892" ANNOTATION_REF="a406891">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>My father became a minister and would be sent to other churches,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406894" ANNOTATION_REF="a406893">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and preach for them, and we would receive some help. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406896" ANNOTATION_REF="a406895">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What was your father’s name? Uh, Buddy Little. Oh, Buddy Little. Uh-huh, Buddy Little was my father.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406898" ANNOTATION_REF="a406897">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>His father’s name was Thomas Little, and that little town of Little was named after him, they used to say. Oh, m-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406900" ANNOTATION_REF="a406899">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>My grandmother was Molly Yeager, Perryman Yeager.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406902" ANNOTATION_REF="a406901">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That grandmother was my father’s mother. And what about your mother?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406904" ANNOTATION_REF="a406903">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>My mother was Miller, on the Jackson Miller side.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406906" ANNOTATION_REF="a406905">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Alice was my mother.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406908" ANNOTATION_REF="a406907">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Alice Miller? Alice Miller. That was my mother.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406910" ANNOTATION_REF="a406909">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They had siblings, too.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406912" ANNOTATION_REF="a406911">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So on what they call the Dawes Roll, did both your parents have a roll number?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406914" ANNOTATION_REF="a406913">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Your mother and your father both. Uh-huh. What they call a roll number.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406916" ANNOTATION_REF="a406915">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>No, I mean on the roll number?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406918" ANNOTATION_REF="a406917">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The enrollment number. Oh, roll number, uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406920" ANNOTATION_REF="a406919">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Did they have one? They had them. All of them, uh-huh. All their siblings, my father, too, had the same.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406922" ANNOTATION_REF="a406921">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So you were saying when he farmed,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406924" ANNOTATION_REF="a406923">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>is that the land that was given to him? Alotted land? Yes, it was. Oh, so it was? Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406926" ANNOTATION_REF="a406925">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Oh, you lived on that land and grew up there? Yeah, we all lived there and grew up there.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406928" ANNOTATION_REF="a406927">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>One house--One house, well, I mean just three rooms. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406930" ANNOTATION_REF="a406929">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That’s where we stayed and grew up. Oh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406932" ANNOTATION_REF="a406931">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So the boys’ chores you said was to milk the cows, and what about you, what were the girls’ chores?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406934" ANNOTATION_REF="a406933">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Oh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406936" ANNOTATION_REF="a406935">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Things that they taught us and that you have to know growing up, they used to say.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406938" ANNOTATION_REF="a406937">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Clean the house, and wash dishes, and a clean kitchen, too, they say,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406940" ANNOTATION_REF="a406939">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>so those were our chores.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406942" ANNOTATION_REF="a406941">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And other things, too. My mother used to be well and about, but she became sick,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406944" ANNOTATION_REF="a406943">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>she got what they called arthritis and became more ill,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406946" ANNOTATION_REF="a406945">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>we were the ones that had to do all the work, like washing, washing clothes. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406948" ANNOTATION_REF="a406947">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah. What is it?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406950" ANNOTATION_REF="a406949">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I forgot how to say "washboard".</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406952" ANNOTATION_REF="a406951">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Is it "sohporokv"? Uh-huh. That’s probably it. We’d boil the water outside and do the wash,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406954" ANNOTATION_REF="a406953">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>we’d clean the clothes. Uh-huh. </ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406956" ANNOTATION_REF="a406955">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That washboard you’re talking about, I have one. I should have brought it. Uh-huh. "This is what she means," I’d have said. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406958" ANNOTATION_REF="a406957">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That’s how we washed things, helping each other, washing, cleaning. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406960" ANNOTATION_REF="a406959">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So wash day, when did you all do wash?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406962" ANNOTATION_REF="a406961">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh, we washed on Sunday. Oh, uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406964" ANNOTATION_REF="a406963">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So did you have one of those great big kettles?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406966" ANNOTATION_REF="a406965">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh-huh, I had that, two of them with water, we’d make a fire outside and heated them up. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406968" ANNOTATION_REF="a406967">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Boiling it. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406970" ANNOTATION_REF="a406969">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And what about the soap? How about the soap?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406972" ANNOTATION_REF="a406971">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They made the soap, too.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406974" ANNOTATION_REF="a406973">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>My mother, my aunts would help. They made soap and such.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406976" ANNOTATION_REF="a406975">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Do you know how to make it?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406978" ANNOTATION_REF="a406977">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh--They call it home-make soap.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406980" ANNOTATION_REF="a406979">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I used to see them make it, but I’ve never made it myself.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406982" ANNOTATION_REF="a406981">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Old grease that’s been setting for a long time,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406984" ANNOTATION_REF="a406983">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>that’s how they used to make those kinds of things.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406986" ANNOTATION_REF="a406985">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Adding the lye. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406988" ANNOTATION_REF="a406987">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So when you look at it, was it sort of yellowish, because of the boiled grease? Uh-huh. That’s what they used? Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406990" ANNOTATION_REF="a406989">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>We saw them when they made them.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406992" ANNOTATION_REF="a406991">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They say that it really cleans you well. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406994" ANNOTATION_REF="a406993">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>But it probably will rub you raw. You know, it burns you. It surely does.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406996" ANNOTATION_REF="a406995">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So you all grew things and sold it</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406998" ANNOTATION_REF="a406997">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>uh--what is it?--that’s how you he received a little money, and they also helped him when he preached. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407000" ANNOTATION_REF="a406999">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He also grew watermelons.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407002" ANNOTATION_REF="a407001">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Watermelons, what they called canteloupe, too, he grew, and tomatoes, </ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407004" ANNOTATION_REF="a407003">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and my mother, too, would grow pumpkins and sold them, too.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407006" ANNOTATION_REF="a407005">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Now [the Indian pumpkin] has gotten scarce, hasn’t it? Now no one does that anymore.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407008" ANNOTATION_REF="a407007">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I looked for one for Thanksgiving and quit. Uh-huh. The ones that seem kind of white.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407010" ANNOTATION_REF="a407009">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>We picked cotton, too.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407012" ANNOTATION_REF="a407011">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So you’ve told us a lot, that’s what we like to hear, like how people lived and how they grew up, as they used to say.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407014" ANNOTATION_REF="a407013">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And also cooking, too,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407016" ANNOTATION_REF="a407015">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>you all were taught how to cook, and you all learned. And I learned that too.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407018" ANNOTATION_REF="a407017">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>As you were saying, we were taught, my younger sisters--is it my younger sisters?--the older ones prepared the food,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407020" ANNOTATION_REF="a407019">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>when my mother became sick, they would cook the food,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407022" ANNOTATION_REF="a407021">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and Juanita and I were the ones that washed the dishes and things.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407024" ANNOTATION_REF="a407023">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Then the chores we mentioned, did the boys go hunting? M-hm, they hunted, too. Oh. They hunted?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407026" ANNOTATION_REF="a407025">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Like for what?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407028" ANNOTATION_REF="a407027">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Like rabbit, deer,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407030" ANNOTATION_REF="a407029">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they would hunt and bring them back. The land that you all lived on, there was plenty [of game]. Uh-huh, that too.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407032" ANNOTATION_REF="a407031">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>We ate well. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407034" ANNOTATION_REF="a407033">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And what they call the "quail", did you all used to eat that, too? Uh, we didn’t eat those. Uh-huh, not those.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407036" ANNOTATION_REF="a407035">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They didn’t hunt for those. They say it’s very good. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407038" ANNOTATION_REF="a407037">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>As for me, I’m protective of those, I think they’re so pretty. I don’t like for them to be killed. I don’t think I’ve ever eaten them.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407040" ANNOTATION_REF="a407039">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So--They’re so small.--Uh-huh, so now you’ve told us a lot of good things, so we’re going to stop a little while.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407042" ANNOTATION_REF="a407041">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah. Nowadays, you don’t ever see someone that is still doing that. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407044" ANNOTATION_REF="a407043">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE/>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407046" ANNOTATION_REF="a407045">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Now then. Again</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407048" ANNOTATION_REF="a407047">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>we have a few more things to talk about, in addition</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407050" ANNOTATION_REF="a407049">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>you all lived very well</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407052" ANNOTATION_REF="a407051">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>as you were growing up, you told us, and now again, like games,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407054" ANNOTATION_REF="a407053">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>you know, various ones that we played when we were children</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407056" ANNOTATION_REF="a407055">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>when we were children they would tell us "You all play", and we would play. And you? Which games do you know?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407058" ANNOTATION_REF="a407057">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh, the games,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407060" ANNOTATION_REF="a407059">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>the one called Drop the handerkerchief,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407062" ANNOTATION_REF="a407061">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>if one had the handkerchief, they’d throw it down,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407064" ANNOTATION_REF="a407063">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they would sit--stand in a circle facing each other, standing looking at each other, one</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407066" ANNOTATION_REF="a407065">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>would take a handkerchief and circle around, and whoever he wanted to drop the handkerchief by, he would, and that person would start running</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407068" ANNOTATION_REF="a407067">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>if that one that’s standing there, if he doesn’t see it, then if another one sees it and picks it up,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407070" ANNOTATION_REF="a407069">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and takes it, and goes around</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407072" ANNOTATION_REF="a407071">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>to where the one that didn’t see was standing,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407074" ANNOTATION_REF="a407073">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>that one would be the one that would be out. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407076" ANNOTATION_REF="a407075">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So as you’re running, you would be chased</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407078" ANNOTATION_REF="a407077">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and you’re going to stand in the space where he stood? Uh-huh. Is that how it is? And if he hasn’t gotten there and you catch him,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407080" ANNOTATION_REF="a407079">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>if you touch him, the one running toward it</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407082" ANNOTATION_REF="a407081">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE/>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407084" ANNOTATION_REF="a407083">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>would be out [of the game]. Oh, uh-huh. So</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407086" ANNOTATION_REF="a407085">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>as it kept going and several went out, the ones in the circle</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407088" ANNOTATION_REF="a407087">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>would get fewer? Just one, just one would be left.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407090" ANNOTATION_REF="a407089">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh-huh. What is it? They used to say London Bridge, too,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407092" ANNOTATION_REF="a407091">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>two girls would be holding each other’s hands raised up--Like this--Uh-huh--like this--both standing like this,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407094" ANNOTATION_REF="a407093">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and they would sing London Bridge. Uh-huh. If they would come underneath-- As one was coming behind, the one [in front] would go out,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407096" ANNOTATION_REF="a407095">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>when one is coming in, that one would go out. Oh, uh-huh. We used to play that.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407098" ANNOTATION_REF="a407097">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>One girl would be standing [caught] in the middle like being under London Bridge. We played things like that-- </ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407100" ANNOTATION_REF="a407099">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What are the other ones?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407102" ANNOTATION_REF="a407101">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE/>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407104" ANNOTATION_REF="a407103">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And they would say Flying Dutchman again they would all stand in a circle, and two of them</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407106" ANNOTATION_REF="a407105">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>would hold hands and go around, when one--</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407108" ANNOTATION_REF="a407107">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they would stand holding hands. If they break through like this,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407110" ANNOTATION_REF="a407109">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>if they break through the ones holding hands, the two that had been holding hands, would take each others hands,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407112" ANNOTATION_REF="a407111">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and would chase them, the two going ahead in the same way</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407114" ANNOTATION_REF="a407113">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>it’s a game played the same. So those ones also keep playing that,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407116" ANNOTATION_REF="a407115">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they kept holding hands until there were a lot of them [pairs]? Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407118" ANNOTATION_REF="a407117">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That’s another game to play--Was that a good game? Uh-huh. A game. A game we used to play.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407120" ANNOTATION_REF="a407119">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>However the games were played,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407122" ANNOTATION_REF="a407121">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>we used to play them. How about the one called Red Light, what about that? Yes. You draw a line on the ground, you know,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407124" ANNOTATION_REF="a407123">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>uh, you use a little stick and draw a line on the ground, is what they used to say. Uh-huh, draw line on the ground. Uh-huh, and they stand th,ere</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407126" ANNOTATION_REF="a407125">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>one goes,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407128" ANNOTATION_REF="a407127">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and if he crosses where the line is, when one says "Red light",</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407130" ANNOTATION_REF="a407129">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they suddenly stop, they stop,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407132" ANNOTATION_REF="a407131">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>when one says "Green light", he goes again, it’s a game like that. So the ones that are standing on the other side</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407134" ANNOTATION_REF="a407133">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>are they the ones that try to catch them? Yes. They try to tag them. Yes. That’s right.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407136" ANNOTATION_REF="a407135">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>If that happens, they would get him out. It was a game to get them out.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407138" ANNOTATION_REF="a407137">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So if they’re playing a gap like that, when they move and when they say "Green light",</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407140" ANNOTATION_REF="a407139">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they would run and chase them. Going across. And then when they said "Red light", all of them would stop. Is that how it was?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407142" ANNOTATION_REF="a407141">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah. That was my favorite game, I think. That one, uh-huh. How about you? Which game did you like to play?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407144" ANNOTATION_REF="a407143">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Flying Dutchman? Probably Flying Dutchman. Oh, if we played it, I never heard of that one. You never heard of it? I never heard of it.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407146" ANNOTATION_REF="a407145">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>We used to play it. Drop the handkerchief, I also like to play. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407148" ANNOTATION_REF="a407147">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And what about Rotten Egg?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407150" ANNOTATION_REF="a407149">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They call it Rotten Egg? I’ve never heard of it, I think.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407152" ANNOTATION_REF="a407151">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh-huh, they used to sit on the ground, the children did, in a circle too, sitting like this, and then one person</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407154" ANNOTATION_REF="a407153">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>would be chosen, and he goes around and picks one, and if it happens to be you, he’d go like this to your head [knocking].</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407156" ANNOTATION_REF="a407155">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>If you ask, "What color?", if I whisper to you "red", or "pink", and so on,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407158" ANNOTATION_REF="a407157">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I’m not sure how I said that, and then it went on to the next one,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407160" ANNOTATION_REF="a407159">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and when he does that to you, if he says "blue", you’d be that color and then it goes on, I think. Oh, I forget, I don’t think I’ve ever played that one either.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407162" ANNOTATION_REF="a407161">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh-huh. And then they would take him by the arms and swing him, and if he falls, they used to call him a rotten egg.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407164" ANNOTATION_REF="a407163">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>But-- I don’t think I’ve ever played that.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407166" ANNOTATION_REF="a407165">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The way we played those, it was like exercise for us, I think. To move your body, is what they say. It was for exercise, that sort of thing.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407168" ANNOTATION_REF="a407167">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And again, what about the rules and things they used to tell us?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407170" ANNOTATION_REF="a407169">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh rules uh</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407172" ANNOTATION_REF="a407171">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>you know, what is it? like if there’s a hole, don’t stick your finger through it</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407174" ANNOTATION_REF="a407173">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>--what is it?--a monster would stick his finger back through, they used to say, how about that? Did you ever hear that? No, I never heard that, I think. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407176" ANNOTATION_REF="a407175">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>How about pointing at a rainbow?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407178" ANNOTATION_REF="a407177">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What about that? What? Pointing at a rainbow. If you see a rainbow, don’t point at it.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407180" ANNOTATION_REF="a407179">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That’s what they used to say. Uh-huh. What did they say would happen?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407182" ANNOTATION_REF="a407181">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What now.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407184" ANNOTATION_REF="a407183">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Did they say your finger would become crooked? That’s what they used to say. Uh-huh. They thought your finger got crooked. That’s it.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407186" ANNOTATION_REF="a407185">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh-huh. Your mouth would get like this.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407188" ANNOTATION_REF="a407187">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Don’t point with it, they used to say. Uh-huh. Something might happen to you, they’d say. M-hm. We don’t point at it.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407190" ANNOTATION_REF="a407189">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Oh, I never heard that. So to point, you’re finger would get crooked, they said.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407192" ANNOTATION_REF="a407191">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And if the hoot owl or uh</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407194" ANNOTATION_REF="a407193">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>horned owl hoots,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407196" ANNOTATION_REF="a407195">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they used to tell us not to imitate it. How about that? Have you heard that before? M-hm. That too.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407198" ANNOTATION_REF="a407197">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They would all swarm around, is kind of what they said. They used to say that.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407200" ANNOTATION_REF="a407199">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>How about when it’s night time, don’t whistle,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407202" ANNOTATION_REF="a407201">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Don’t go around whistling, is what they used to tell us. How about that? I’ve heard that.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407204" ANNOTATION_REF="a407203">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I don’t remember what they said it meant. M-hm. Or maybe they’d say that something would whistle back at you.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407206" ANNOTATION_REF="a407205">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They would whistle back at you is what they said, I think. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407208" ANNOTATION_REF="a407207">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>When a woman is going to have a child, or</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407210" ANNOTATION_REF="a407209">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>she’s going to add on to her family, so they would say she was pregnant, what about that? There were rules about that. Do you know about that?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407212" ANNOTATION_REF="a407211">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Like on the bed--right way--</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407214" ANNOTATION_REF="a407213">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>don’t lie on it, don’t lie sideways, they say. M-hm. They would say like that. Again,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407216" ANNOTATION_REF="a407215">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I used to hear that rule. M-hm. And that tree--I mean, I said tree--door</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407218" ANNOTATION_REF="a407217">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>the open space, I mean, what is it? They used to say not to stand in the doorway. Yes, they used to say not to stand there.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407220" ANNOTATION_REF="a407219">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>M-hm. Also--</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407222" ANNOTATION_REF="a407221">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Also,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407224" ANNOTATION_REF="a407223">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>not to sleep too much.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407226" ANNOTATION_REF="a407225">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Don’t sleep and sleep, they’d say, and they’d tell us, children--when a baby is going to be born, we would drift off to sleep,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407228" ANNOTATION_REF="a407227">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>on that day</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407230" ANNOTATION_REF="a407229">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>you might have a hard time [in labor], is why they were telling us, is what I thought. Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407232" ANNOTATION_REF="a407231">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Don’t sleep more than you should, they used to say. Oh, uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407234" ANNOTATION_REF="a407233">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I’ve never heard that. They were probably right. Uh-huh. Just sleeping, after she has the baby, she’ll always be sleeping,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407236" ANNOTATION_REF="a407235">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they didn’t want her to do that, is what they meant. Yes. So again</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407238" ANNOTATION_REF="a407237">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>we’re not to go to a funeral [when you’re pregnant], is what they used to say. That too, they tell us not to go.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407240" ANNOTATION_REF="a407239">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That too was a rule. "Don’t look," they said, during the viewing, don’t look, they said. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407242" ANNOTATION_REF="a407241">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That woman might be overcome, and--what is it?--</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407244" ANNOTATION_REF="a407243">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>people lose consciousness, don’t they? If they see someone like that. I wonder if they thought it might happen like that?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407246" ANNOTATION_REF="a407245">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Her breathing might be cut off and she’d be short on air, is that what they were thinking? Yes.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407248" ANNOTATION_REF="a407247">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That’s why they said that.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407250" ANNOTATION_REF="a407249">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That was a rule they used to say. I’ve never heard that, I think. Oh, uh-huh. When she becomes overwhelmed, the baby would be overwhelmed as well, that’s sort of like what they used to say.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407252" ANNOTATION_REF="a407251">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407254" ANNOTATION_REF="a407253">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The rules, some don’t mind them,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407256" ANNOTATION_REF="a407255">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>don’t be saying that it will be okay, if they tell you a rule, listen to them,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407258" ANNOTATION_REF="a407257">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>they are teaching you, is what they used to say. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407260" ANNOTATION_REF="a407259">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They seem to have been right. It’s good to stand by those, is what they say.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407262" ANNOTATION_REF="a407261">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then they didn’t tell us over and over, we just knew those rules, didn’t we?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407264" ANNOTATION_REF="a407263">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The things you’ve said, I know some about them because they told me.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407266" ANNOTATION_REF="a407265">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Didn’t they just want us to know these things?, I wonder.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407268" ANNOTATION_REF="a407267">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>You knew all of this, too, and myself, I knew some, too, didn’t I? Uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407270" ANNOTATION_REF="a407269">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh-huh. I think everyone knew of these rules within themselves.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407272" ANNOTATION_REF="a407271">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then again--what is it?--like the churches or</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407274" ANNOTATION_REF="a407273">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>grounds, what they used to call stompdance, dances and such, how about that, which one did your parents start from?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407276" ANNOTATION_REF="a407275">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Uh--At first, that stompdance</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407278" ANNOTATION_REF="a407277">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I never heard that they went to that, but these elders</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407280" ANNOTATION_REF="a407279">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>used to go to the fiddle dances when they had them. But after a while,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407282" ANNOTATION_REF="a407281">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>it may have turned into a stompdance. Oh. I don’t know, but when my later father would talk about the fiddle dance,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407284" ANNOTATION_REF="a407283">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>he played it [the fiddle], and they danced. That’s where we went.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407286" ANNOTATION_REF="a407285">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>As time went on they may have gone to a ground, but my late mother said that my aunt Buster Fife</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407288" ANNOTATION_REF="a407287">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>was very good at shaking shells. Oh, m-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407290" ANNOTATION_REF="a407289">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They were shell shakers, they said, that’s what I used to hear.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407292" ANNOTATION_REF="a407291">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So your father played what they call a fiddle, was it an instrument like a violin?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407294" ANNOTATION_REF="a407293">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Fiddle? Oh fiddle? Fiddle. Yes, the fiddle. The way they danced,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407296" ANNOTATION_REF="a407295">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>a chair like this--yeah, a chair standing,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407298" ANNOTATION_REF="a407297">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>a chair--they set a regular chair up, like this, and would stand behind it and dance</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407300" ANNOTATION_REF="a407299">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and probably went around it. That’s the kind of dance</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407302" ANNOTATION_REF="a407301">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>that they danced, they said.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407304" ANNOTATION_REF="a407303">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That’s what I heard them talk about. So how did your father learn how to play the fiddle?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407306" ANNOTATION_REF="a407305">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Oh, just--</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407308" ANNOTATION_REF="a407307">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>he wasn’t taught, he himself learned by himself. Or listening to it. Uh-huh. From then on. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407310" ANNOTATION_REF="a407309">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>As time went on, when my late father’s father passed away,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407312" ANNOTATION_REF="a407311">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>his mother married a white person,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407314" ANNOTATION_REF="a407313">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>and [my father] as raised not knowing the Seminole language, when he was about [fourteen?]</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407316" ANNOTATION_REF="a407315">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>he learned our Seminole language and went on to become a preacher, they said. Oh, m-hm, m-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407318" ANNOTATION_REF="a407317">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He also became a preacher and was sent to various churches,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407320" ANNOTATION_REF="a407319">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>he preached and we went with him and grew up. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407322" ANNOTATION_REF="a407321">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So you all mostly went to church instead? Yes, we went there. Oh. And still do?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407324" ANNOTATION_REF="a407323">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>You still go now? Yes, the rest--well, the others don’t go, but</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407326" ANNOTATION_REF="a407325">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>my sister Juanita and I still go together.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407328" ANNOTATION_REF="a407327">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Which one are you members of?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407330" ANNOTATION_REF="a407329">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Which one your family-- your church-- The church, we were raised in Hitchiti church.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407332" ANNOTATION_REF="a407331">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Oh. My dad-- my late grandpa Thomas Little was the one who started it, they used to say. He started it. Oh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407334" ANNOTATION_REF="a407333">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So you both still go there? Yes, there. Oh, that’s very good. We grew up going there.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407336" ANNOTATION_REF="a407335">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I still go there. M-hm, m-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407338" ANNOTATION_REF="a407337">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>My sister goes to that Snake Creek church. Oh, is that where she goes? Yes, she goes there instead.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407340" ANNOTATION_REF="a407339">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Oh. I go, I still go to Hitchiti. M-hm, m-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407342" ANNOTATION_REF="a407341">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I may be the oldest one going there. Oh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407344" ANNOTATION_REF="a407343">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I’m the only one that’s left. Uh-huh. Yes.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407346" ANNOTATION_REF="a407345">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then other things like making quilts,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407348" ANNOTATION_REF="a407347">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>or like making beads,</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407350" ANNOTATION_REF="a407349">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>or other things like art that others know how to do, how about you, do you have any hobbies?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407352" ANNOTATION_REF="a407351">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I make quilts too, and I also make clothes.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407354" ANNOTATION_REF="a407353">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>M-hm. I also make ribbon shirts if they ask for them. M-hm.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407356" ANNOTATION_REF="a407355">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I make things like patchwork, too. Oh, you make that too?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407358" ANNOTATION_REF="a407357">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Did you learn from your mother, or how did you learn that?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407360" ANNOTATION_REF="a407359">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I think I just learned by myself. Oh, teaching yourself. Teaching myself, yeah. Oh, uh-huh.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407362" ANNOTATION_REF="a407361">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I think those are hard to make. Yes.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
